Mechanical quantities and English–Portuguese vocabulary (@mech-language: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Engineering-Statics-Baker-and-Haynes.lingua#r_3DXGKGQSPPA9YDNH2WSB8XRN80", #source "../sources/FUNdaMENTALS-of-Design-Slocum.lingua#r_58Q6VQJ3FXXGXRBJ3DK0AVC3WQ", #mechanical-engineering "Parts-interfaces-and-the-path-of-a-load.lingua#r_0GDXXPH3HG15NE437QEDYMSTZ8") { r_4P2MRH0T3YANEA9BHGVW2VQV2R
**Read:** [Engineering Statics — Baker and Haynes](../sources/Engineering-Statics-Baker-and-Haynes.lingua#r_3DXGKGQSPPA9YDNH2WSB8XRN80), chapters 1–2, with the relevant component names in [FUNdaMENTALS of Design — Alexander Slocum](../sources/FUNdaMENTALS-of-Design-Slocum.lingua#r_58Q6VQJ3FXXGXRBJ3DK0AVC3WQ). Learn the physical meaning alongside the English and Portuguese terms.

Useful pairs include force/força, moment or torque/momento ou torque, stress/tensão mecânica, strain/deformação específica, displacement/deslocamento, stiffness/rigidez, strength/resistência, shaft/eixo ou árvore, bearing/mancal ou rolamento, clearance/folga and fit/ajuste. Usage depends on context: a rolling bearing is one kind of bearing, and electrical voltage is not mechanical stress despite the Portuguese word tensão.

Angles in radians are dimensionless in dimensional analysis, but their interpretation still matters. At 600 revolutions/minute, angular speed is 20π rad/s. A 10 N·m torque at that speed transfers about 628.319 W when torque and angular velocity have the same direction. Equal dimensions do not make torque and energy interchangeable physical quantities.

**Work:** Translate a short equipment description both ways without dropping units or conditions. Explain stiffness versus strength with a spring and a brittle object, then identify what evidence would be needed to quantify either claim. Build vocabulary around the parts you actually study.

**Return:** [Mechanical engineering and machine design](../Mechanical-engineering-and-machine-design.lingua#r_0017YZ63HZBZ4P4WD8DECVWE4R).
